//! C++ FFI surface for the configuration loader.
//!
//! Layout:
//! - **Opaque `OptionalT` wrappers** carry optional scalars across the
//!   boundary. Each wraps a native Rust `Option<T>` and exposes `has_value()`,
//!   `value()` (throws if absent), and `value_or(fallback)` to C++. Uniform
//!   API across primitive scalars and `String`.
//! - The schema structs (`Config`, `Server`, …) are opaque Rust types whose
//!   getters are auto-generated by `#[derive(ConfigEntries)]`.
//! - Parse entry points return `Box<ParseOutcome>` — `std::expected`-shaped
//!   wrapper with `has_value() / has_error() / value() / error()`.
//!
//! ## Phase-2 additions
//!
//! - **cxx-shared enums** mirror data-less schema enums (`RelayMode`,
//!   `SafetyLevel`, `JournalMode`, `Synchronous`, `TempStore`, `SqdbBackend`,
//!   `InsightServer`, `Protocol`) so both sides see the same variant set.
//!   Conversions go through `From<schema::Foo> for ffi::Foo` helpers.
//! - **`OptionalT` wrappers** follow Pattern A. For polymorphic enums
//!   (`LedgerHistory`, `FetchDepth`, `NetworkId`, `NodeSize`, `PortLimit`) a
//!   `kind()` discriminant plus per-variant accessor(s) is used.
//! - **`OptionalNodeDb`** is the tagged-enum view over `NodeDb` (NuDB |
//!   RocksDB). Variant-specific fields return absent `OptionalU32` when the
//!   wrong variant is active — cleaner than discriminating from C++.
//! - **`Server::ports`** is exposed via `port_names()` / `has_port()` /
//!   `port(name)` (Pattern E).

#![allow(unused_imports)] // cxx-bridge resolves these from the parent module.

